HST Office: Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V copy and paste formatting in HST Slides, as in the reference suite (owner
decision 2026-11-15).

- .uno:HstCopyFormat (SID_HST_COPY_FORMAT) takes the formats of the selected shape, or of the selected text while
  editing, with the Clone Formatting brush's core (SdrObjEditView::TakeFormatPaintBrush) but without its mouse mode.
  .uno:HstPasteFormat (SID_HST_PASTE_FORMAT) applies them (ApplyFormatPaintBrush) to every selected shape, or to the
  selected text (the word at the cursor without a selection; paragraph formats only for whole paragraphs, as the
  brush), as one undo action. The copy stays until the next copy and belongs to its document: it is dropped when
  that document closes, and pasting into another document does nothing (as Writer's keys).
- sd/source/ui/{inc,func}/HstFormatCopyPaste: the commands; DrawViewShell::FuSupport runs them (not FuTemporary,
  which would end text editing) and GetMenuState disables them without a selection, without a copy of this
  document's formats, or (paste) for a read-only document. app.hrc, sdraw.sdi, drviewsh.sdi, Library_sd.mk;
  DrawImpressCommands.xcu labels and their Vietnamese in UI.po.
- Keys, HST Slides only (macOS Cmd+Shift+C / Cmd+Shift+V, the Mac edition's keys too): Ctrl+Shift+V was Paste
  Special, which stays on Ctrl+Alt+V, the ribbon and the Edit menu.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); new files MPL-2.0 like the module.
Test: scripts/check-keytips-parity.py, tests/runtime/check-shortcut-parity-runtime.py.
